From 91058379ca59c4848cd8dee0989c2d83e363a1d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 8 May 2026 08:24:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] freedreno/a2xx: invalidate L2 texture cache at every
 batch start

Patch 0038 made the cmdstream byte-identical between cold-boot and
post-LSM-kill kmscube, but visual residuals persist (cube faces fade
in/out, glmark2 texture broken on first cycle, gears ghost-quad).

cffdump comparison of cold vs post-LSM cmdstreams confirmed Mesa is
emitting the right cmdstream in both cases - same opcodes, same
addresses, same BO references. The leak is below cmdstream level.

Root-cause analysis points to the GPU L2 texture cache (TC). Kernel-
side gpummu_unmap invalidates the MMU TLB
(MH_MMU_INVALIDATE_INVALIDATE_TC = MMU translation cache for the
texture client) but does NOT invalidate the L2 texture cache, which
is a separate HW unit accessed via TC_CNTL_STATUS_L2_INVALIDATE.

L2 TC is keyed by physical address. When a GLES client inherits
CMA-allocated BOs at physical pages a previous client just vacated,
the GPU TC may still hold the previous client's texture data at
those physical addresses. CPU writes via glTexImage2D don't
invalidate GPU TC, so the next GPU sample returns stale data.

Mesa freedreno's a2xx path already invalidates L2 inside
fd2_emit_tile_mem2gmem (before the FB-as-texture blit), but not on
batch boundaries / context switches in general. Add an L2 invalidate
+ WFI to fd2_emit_restore so every batch start gets a clean texture
cache.

Cost: one CP packet per batch, plus a single WFI to wait for
invalidate completion. Aligned with the natural state-restore
rhythm; effectively free when no stale entries exist.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
(cherry picked from commit 9d9133f2acc41cbf3737eb3a844e681c9ac7fe77)
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c | 33 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
index 31f45ce3567..05a69b12a71 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
@@ -473,6 +473,39 @@ fd2_emit_restore(struct fd_context *ctx, struct fd_ringbuffer *ring)
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_INVALIDATE_STATE, 1);
    OUT_RING(ring, 0x00007fff);
 
+   /*
+    * Invalidate the L2 texture cache (TC) at every batch start.
+    *
+    * Mesa's dirty-flag tracking + patch 0038 (mark all state dirty after
+    * GMEM tile setup/resolve/sysmem_prep) ensures the cmdstream emits
+    * the correct register values across batch boundaries, but the GPU
+    * L2 texture cache is keyed by physical address and persists across
+    * processes. Kernel-side gpummu_unmap invalidates the MMU TLB
+    * (MH_MMU_INVALIDATE_TC = MMU translation cache) but NOT the L2
+    * texture cache.
+    *
+    * When a GLES client (e.g. kmscube) inherits CMA-allocated BOs at
+    * physical pages a previous client (e.g. luna-surfacemanager) just
+    * vacated, the GPU TC may still hold the previous client's texture
+    * data at those physical addresses. CPU writes via glTexImage2D do
+    * not invalidate GPU TC, so the GPU samples stale data.
+    *
+    * Symptoms on Adreno 220 / HP TouchPad: kmscube cube faces fade in
+    * and out across runs after LSM exits; LSM glyph text shows wrong
+    * pixels; glmark2 texture test renders incorrectly on first
+    * post-LSM cycle.
+    *
+    * Invalidating L2 at batch start (where fd2_emit_restore runs) is
+    * the cheapest correct fix - one packet, no perf cost when there's
+    * nothing to invalidate, and once-per-batch frequency aligns with
+    * the natural state-restore rhythm.
+    */
+   OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A2XX_TC_CNTL_STATUS, 1);
+   OUT_RING(ring, A2XX_TC_CNTL_STATUS_L2_INVALIDATE);
+
+   /* Wait for L2 invalidate to complete before any subsequent fetch. */
+   OUT_WFI(ring);
+
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 2);
    OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_SQ_VS_CONST));
    OUT_RING(ring, A2XX_SQ_VS_CONST_BASE(VS_CONST_BASE) |
-- 
